#### 1.2.4 Overall quality objectives for pharmacovigilance
The overall quality objectives of a pharmacovigilance system are:
- Complying with the legal requirements for pharmacovigilance tasks and responsibilities;
- Preventing harm from adverse reactions in humans arising from the use of authorized
pharmaceutical products within or outside the terms of marketing authorization or from
occupational exposure;
- Promoting the safe and effective use of pharmaceutical products, in particular through
providing timely information about the safety of pharmaceutical products to patients,
healthcare professionals and the public;
- Contributing to the protection of patients and public health[EDA Document: Guideline_on_Good_Pharmacovigilance_Practice_Egypt_2026.md]

