#### 5.2.11 RMP part VI “Summary of the risk management plan”
The RMP summary shall be updated when important changes are introduced into the full RMP.
Changes shall be considered important if they relate to the following: new important identified or
potential risks or important changes to or removal of a safety concern; inclusion or removal of
additional risk minimization measures or routine risk minimization activities recommending
specific clinical measures to address the risk; major changes to the pharmacovigilance plan (e.g.
addition of new studies or completion of ongoing studies).
The summary of the RMP part VI shall be consistent with the information presented in RMP part
II modules SVII, SVIII and RMP parts III, IV and V. It shall contain the following information:
-    The pharmaceutical product and what it is authorized for;
-    Summary of safety concerns and missing information;
-    Routine and additional risk minimization measures;
-    Additional pharmacovigilance activities.[EDA Document: Guideline_on_Good_Pharmacovigilance_Practice_Egypt_2026.md]

