# Guideline on Good Pharmacovigilance Practice (GVP) in Egypt for Pharmaceutical Products — RAG Knowledge Base

**Document Type**: Regulatory and Technical Guideline / Pharmacovigilance Knowledge Base for Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG)
**Issuing Body**: Central Administration of Pharmaceutical Care; General Administration for Pharmaceutical Vigilance
**Jurisdiction**: Arab Republic of Egypt
**Code**: EDREX:GL.CAP.care.015
**Version**: Version 3 / 2026
**Issue Date**: 01/07/2026
**Effective Date**: 09/07/2026
**Scope**: Good pharmacovigilance practice for pharmaceutical products for human use, including biological products
**Primary Regulated Entity**: Marketing authorization holders and applicants
**Regulatory Authority**: Egyptian Drug Authority (EDA)
**Optimization**: Semantic chunking, explicit metadata, chapter/subchapter hierarchy, preserved regulatory wording, no HTML tables

**Metadata Tags**: Pharmacovigilance, GVP, EDA, Egypt, Marketing Authorization Holder, MAH, Safety, Adverse Event, ICSR, PBRER, Signal Management, Risk Management Plan, RMP, PV Inspection, PV Audit, Safety Communication, Biological Products, Safety, Adverse Event, ICSR, PBRER, Signal Management, Risk Management Plan, RMP, PV Inspection, PV Audit, Safety Communication, Biological Products

