## 2. Policy and Implementation Framework
### 2.1 Policy Purpose

The Arabic policy section defines the policy as the use of antibiotics to prevent surgical-site infection.

**Policy Goals**:
- Reduce irrational antimicrobial use.
- Reduce adverse effects caused by inappropriate antimicrobial use.
- Prevent deaths related to surgical-site infection.
- Reduce hospital length of stay and healthcare cost.
- Reduce emergence of antimicrobial-resistant strains.

**Policy Scope**:
- Identify antimicrobial agents used for surgical-site-infection prophylaxis according to the surgical procedure.
- Define adult and pediatric doses.
- Define the timing of administration before surgery.
- Distribute the protocol to healthcare institutions with surgical operating departments.
- Implement the protocol according to each hospital’s approved policies.[EDA Document: National Guidance for Antimicrobial Prophylaxis in Surgery — RAG Knowledge Base.md]

