## 5. Surgical Wound Classification

The Centers for Disease Control and Prevention identifies four surgical wound categories.
### 5.1 Clean Wound

- An uninfected operative wound with no inflammation.
- The respiratory, alimentary, genital, or uninfected urinary tract is not entered.
- The wound is primarily closed and, if necessary, drained with a closed drainage system.[EDA Document: National Guidance for Antimicrobial Prophylaxis in Surgery — RAG Knowledge Base.md]

