[Section: 7.3 Intraoperative Redosing]
Give the preoperative dose within 60 minutes before surgical incision.
- Fluoroquinolones and vancomycin require administration over 1–2 hours; begin these agents within 120 minutes before incision.
### 7.3 Intraoperative Redosing

- Measure the redosing interval from administration of the preoperative dose, not from the beginning of the procedure.
- Redose when the procedure exceeds two half-lives of the antimicrobial.
- Redose when there is excessive blood loss, defined in the guidance as more than 1,500 mL.
- Redosing may be needed when factors shorten the antimicrobial half-life, such as extensive burns.
- Redosing may not be needed when the antimicrobial half-life is prolonged, such as in renal insufficiency or renal failure.[EDA Document: National Guidance for Antimicrobial Prophylaxis in Surgery — RAG Knowledge Base.md]

