### 7.4 Duration of Prophylaxis

- Use a shortened postoperative course whenever possible.
- A single dose or continuation for less than 24 hours is recommended for many procedures.
- Many procedures do not require postoperative prophylaxis.
- If prophylaxis is continued after closure, limit it to 24 hours or less unless a procedure-specific exception is stated.

