## 9. Neonatal Surgical Prophylaxis
### 9.1 Neonatal Procedures With One-Dose Cefazolin

**Procedures listed**:
- Biliary tract or choledochal-cyst surgery.
- Congenital diaphragmatic hernia repair.
- Duodenal atresia surgery.
- Gastrostomy.
- Nissen fundoplication.
- Liver biopsy.
- Head and neck surgery.

**Recommended**: One dose of cefazolin in neonates without beta-lactam allergy.[EDA Document: National Guidance for Antimicrobial Prophylaxis in Surgery — RAG Knowledge Base.md]

