[Section: 10.1 Ampicillin–Sulbactam]
he values below reproduce the supplied guidance. Verify weight, indication, maximum dose, allergy status, renal function, institutional formulary, and current drug information before administration.
### 10.1 Ampicillin–Sulbactam

- **Adult dose**: 3 g, consisting of ampicillin 2 g and sulbactam 1 g.
- **Pediatric dose**: 50 mg/kg of the ampicillin component.
- **Redosing interval**: 2 hours from initiation of the preoperative dose.
- **If continued after surgery**: 3 g every 6 hours, up to 3 doses.[EDA Document: National Guidance for Antimicrobial Prophylaxis in Surgery — RAG Knowledge Base.md]

