## 11. RAG Retrieval Metadata and Chunking Guidance
### 11.1 Recommended Chunking Strategy

- Split primarily on H2 and H3 headings.
- Keep each procedure-specific recommendation as a coherent chunk.
- Keep the recommended regimen, allergy alternative, and notes in the same chunk.
- Keep each antimicrobial dose and redosing record as an atomic chunk.
- Include the parent specialty and patient population in each chunk.
- Preserve units, timing windows, redosing intervals, and postoperative durations exactly.
- Avoid splitting a dose from its population qualifier or special note.[EDA Document: National Guidance for Antimicrobial Prophylaxis in Surgery — RAG Knowledge Base.md]

