### 11.3 Consistency Notes

- Use “surgical-site infection” and the abbreviation “SSI” consistently.
- Use “Staphylococcus aureus,” “MSSA,” and “MRSA” consistently.
- Use “preoperative dose” for the dose before incision.
- Use “redosing interval” for intraoperative repeat dosing.
- Distinguish prophylaxis from treatment of established infection.
- Keep procedure names and antimicrobial names explicit for semantic retrieval.
- Do not interpret an alternative regimen as equivalent for every patient; retain the source’s qualifying notes.
- Do not infer a missing dose or duration when the source does not state one.

