- `effective_reference`: May 2021 for active ingredients; July/August 2024 for trade-name products
### 3.4 Consistency Notes

- Keep generic names, trade names, strengths, routes, and pack limits as separate searchable fields.
- Do not generalize a warning from one formulation to another formulation of the same ingredient.
- Preserve age restrictions and “medical supervision” requirements exactly.
- Preserve warnings about drowsiness, renal impairment, pregnancy, sodium restriction, hypersensitivity, and labeling.
- Where the PDF extraction wraps a record over multiple lines, associate the continuation lines with the nearest preceding numbered record.
- Verify spelling, strength, formulation, and current approval status against the latest official EDA source before production use.

