(...continued from previous section: "Use with caution; consult a physician.")[Drug: Enalapril]
Indications / Uses: Hypertension; symptomatic heart failure (as an adjunct to diuretics and other therapy); asymptomatic left ventricular dysfunction.[Drug: Enalapril]
Adult Dosage & Administration: Adults: 5–20 mg once or twice daily, titrated according to blood pressure response and tolerability.

(...continued from previous section: "Hypertension; symptomatic heart failure (as an adjunct to diuretics and other therapy); asymptomatic left ventricular dysfunction.")[Drug: Enalapril]
Contraindications: Pregnancy; history of angioedema related to previous ACE inhibitor therapy; bilateral renal artery stenosis; known hypersensitivity.

(...continued from previous section: "Adults: 5–20 mg once or twice daily, titrated according to blood pressure response and tolerability.")[Drug: Enalapril]
Warnings & Precautions: Risk of angioedema (can occur at any time during treatment, including the face, lips, tongue, and airway — discontinue immediately and seek emergency care if it occurs); risk of hyperkalemia and renal impairment, especially with renal artery stenosis, volume depletion, or concurrent potassium-sparing agents; persistent dry cough is a common, non-dangerous class effect.

(...continued from previous section: "Pregnancy; history of angioedema related to previous ACE inhibitor therapy; bilateral renal artery stenosis; known hypersensitivity.")[Drug: Enalapril]
Common Side Effects: Dry cough, dizziness, headache, hypotension.

(...continued from previous section: "isk of hyperkalemia and renal impairment, especially with renal artery stenosis, volume depletion, or concurrent potassium-sparing agents; persistent dry cough is a common, non-dangerous class effect.")[Drug: Enalapril]
Serious Side Effects / Seek Medical Help: Angioedema, hyperkalemia, acute renal failure.

(...continued from previous section: "Dry cough, dizziness, headache, hypotension.")[Drug: Enalapril]
Drug Interactions: Potassium-sparing diuretics/potassium supplements (hyperkalemia); NSAIDs (reduced antihypertensive effect, renal risk); lithium (increased levels); avoid combination with ARBs or aliskiren.

(...continued from previous section: "Angioedema, hyperkalemia, acute renal failure.")[Drug: Enalapril]
Use in Pregnancy: Contraindicated (associated with fetal and neonatal injury, particularly in the second and third trimesters).

(...continued from previous section: "Potassium-sparing diuretics/potassium supplements (hyperkalemia); NSAIDs (reduced antihypertensive effect, renal risk); lithium (increased levels); avoid combination with ARBs or aliskiren.")[Drug: Enalapril]
Use in Breastfeeding (Lactation): Use with caution; consult a physician for alternatives.

(...continued from previous section: "Contraindicated (associated with fetal and neonatal injury, particularly in the second and third trimesters).")[Drug: Enalapril]
