(...continued from previous section: "Use with caution; consult a physician for alternatives.")[Drug: Hydrochlorothiazide]
Indications / Uses: Hypertension (alone or in combination); edema associated with heart failure, hepatic, or renal disease.[Drug: Hydrochlorothiazide]
Adult Dosage & Administration: Adults: 12.5–25 mg once daily, usually in the morning.

(...continued from previous section: "Hypertension (alone or in combination); edema associated with heart failure, hepatic, or renal disease.")[Drug: Hydrochlorothiazide]
Contraindications: Anuria; known hypersensitivity to thiazides or sulfonamide-derived drugs (relative, case-dependent).

(...continued from previous section: "Adults: 12.5–25 mg once daily, usually in the morning.")[Drug: Hydrochlorothiazide]
Warnings & Precautions: Can cause electrolyte disturbances (hypokalemia, hyponatremia, hypomagnesemia), hyperglycemia, hyperuricemia (may precipitate gout), and photosensitivity; monitor electrolytes periodically, especially in the elderly or with concomitant diuretic/ACE-inhibitor therapy.

(...continued from previous section: "Anuria; known hypersensitivity to thiazides or sulfonamide-derived drugs (relative, case-dependent).")[Drug: Hydrochlorothiazide]
Common Side Effects: Increased urination, dizziness, mild electrolyte changes.

(...continued from previous section: "magnesemia), hyperglycemia, hyperuricemia (may precipitate gout), and photosensitivity; monitor electrolytes periodically, especially in the elderly or with concomitant diuretic/ACE-inhibitor therapy.")[Drug: Hydrochlorothiazide]
Serious Side Effects / Seek Medical Help: Severe hyponatremia, hypokalemia-related arrhythmia, rare pancreatitis.

(...continued from previous section: "Increased urination, dizziness, mild electrolyte changes.")[Drug: Hydrochlorothiazide]
Drug Interactions: Lithium (increased lithium levels/toxicity); NSAIDs (reduced diuretic/antihypertensive effect); digoxin (hypokalemia increases digoxin toxicity risk).

(...continued from previous section: "Severe hyponatremia, hypokalemia-related arrhythmia, rare pancreatitis.")[Drug: Hydrochlorothiazide]
Use in Pregnancy: Generally avoided unless specifically indicated; consult a physician.

(...continued from previous section: "Lithium (increased lithium levels/toxicity); NSAIDs (reduced diuretic/antihypertensive effect); digoxin (hypokalemia increases digoxin toxicity risk).")[Drug: Hydrochlorothiazide]
Use in Breastfeeding (Lactation): Use with caution; may reduce milk volume; consult a physician.

(...continued from previous section: "Generally avoided unless specifically indicated; consult a physician.")[Drug: Hydrochlorothiazide]
