(...continued from previous section: "Use with caution; consult a physician.")[Drug: Oral Rehydration Salts (ORS)]
Indications / Uses: Prevention and treatment of dehydration resulting from diarrhea, vomiting, or excessive fluid loss.[Drug: Oral Rehydration Salts (ORS)]
Adult Dosage & Administration: Reconstitute strictly according to the water volume stated on the product label; give in small, frequent sips, with the total volume guided by degree of dehydration and body weight (follow local rehydration protocol/pharmacist guidance).

(...continued from previous section: "Prevention and treatment of dehydration resulting from diarrhea, vomiting, or excessive fluid loss.")[Drug: Oral Rehydration Salts (ORS)]
Contraindications: Severe dehydration requiring intravenous fluids; intestinal obstruction or paralytic ileus; persistent vomiting preventing oral intake; anuria/severe renal failure without medical supervision.

(...continued from previous section: "e water volume stated on the product label; give in small, frequent sips, with the total volume guided by degree of dehydration and body weight (follow local rehydration protocol/pharmacist guidance).")[Drug: Oral Rehydration Salts (ORS)]
Warnings & Precautions: Preparing the solution with too little water (over-concentration) can cause hypernatremia, especially dangerous in infants; use only drinking-quality water; prepare fresh solution and discard any unused portion after 24 hours (or per label).

(...continued from previous section: "Severe dehydration requiring intravenous fluids; intestinal obstruction or paralytic ileus; persistent vomiting preventing oral intake; anuria/severe renal failure without medical supervision.")[Drug: Oral Rehydration Salts (ORS)]
Common Side Effects: Well tolerated when prepared and dosed correctly.

(...continued from previous section: "ter (over-concentration) can cause hypernatremia, especially dangerous in infants; use only drinking-quality water; prepare fresh solution and discard any unused portion after 24 hours (or per label).")[Drug: Oral Rehydration Salts (ORS)]
Serious Side Effects / Seek Medical Help: Electrolyte imbalance (hypernatremia/hyponatremia) if prepared or dosed incorrectly.

(...continued from previous section: "Well tolerated when prepared and dosed correctly.")[Drug: Oral Rehydration Salts (ORS)]
Drug Interactions: No clinically significant drug interactions in typical use.

(...continued from previous section: "Electrolyte imbalance (hypernatremia/hyponatremia) if prepared or dosed incorrectly.")[Drug: Oral Rehydration Salts (ORS)]
Use in Pregnancy: Safe for use in pregnancy.

(...continued from previous section: "No clinically significant drug interactions in typical use.")[Drug: Oral Rehydration Salts (ORS)]
Use in Breastfeeding (Lactation): Safe for use while breastfeeding.

(...continued from previous section: "Safe for use in pregnancy.")[Drug: Oral Rehydration Salts (ORS)]
Storage Instructions: Unopened sachets: room temperature, protect from moisture. Reconstituted solution: use within 24 hours; refrigerate between uses if possible, discard remainder after 24 hours.

(...continued from previous section: "Safe for use while breastfeeding.")[Drug: Cetirizine]
Indications / Uses: Allergic rhinitis (seasonal and perennial), allergic conjunctivitis, chronic idiopathic urticaria.[Drug: Cetirizine]
Adult Dosage & Administration: Adults: 10 mg once daily.

(...continued from previous section: "Allergic rhinitis (seasonal and perennial), allergic conjunctivitis, chronic idiopathic urticaria.")[Drug: Cetirizine]
Contraindications: Known hypersensitivity to cetirizine, hydroxyzine, or piperazine derivatives; severe renal impairment requires dose adjustment.

(...continued from previous section: "Adults: 10 mg once daily.")[Drug: Cetirizine]
Warnings & Precautions: Mild sedation can occur (less than first-generation antihistamines but not negligible) — use caution when driving or operating machinery until individual response is known; dose reduction needed in renal or significant hepatic impairment.

(...continued from previous section: "Known hypersensitivity to cetirizine, hydroxyzine, or piperazine derivatives; severe renal impairment requires dose adjustment.")[Drug: Cetirizine]
Common Side Effects: Mild drowsiness, dry mouth, headache, fatigue.

(...continued from previous section: "st-generation antihistamines but not negligible) — use caution when driving or operating machinery until individual response is known; dose reduction needed in renal or significant hepatic impairment.")[Drug: Cetirizine]
Serious Side Effects / Seek Medical Help: Rare hypersensitivity reactions.

(...continued from previous section: "Mild drowsiness, dry mouth, headache, fatigue.")[Drug: Cetirizine]
Drug Interactions: Additive sedation with alcohol or other CNS depressants.

(...continued from previous section: "Rare hypersensitivity reactions.")[Drug: Cetirizine]
Use in Pregnancy: Generally considered to have a low risk profile; use if clinically needed.

(...continued from previous section: "Additive sedation with alcohol or other CNS depressants.")[Drug: Cetirizine]
Use in Breastfeeding (Lactation): Generally considered compatible; monitor infant for drowsiness.

(...continued from previous section: "Generally considered to have a low risk profile; use if clinically needed.")[Drug: Cetirizine]
